<title>NETHERLANDS: Pakhoed shares jump on profit news.</title>
<headline>Pakhoed shares jump on profit news.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-07-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Dutch tank storage and shipping group Pakhoed NV rose more than six percent in early trading after news of higher first half profits and an upgrade of the firm's full year forecast.</p>
<p>The shares were trading at 75.30 guilders at 0735 GMT, up 4.80 guilders, after touching a year's high of 75.50.</p>
<p>Pakhoed on Wednesday said net profit from ordinary operations rose 75 percent to about 103 million guilders in the first half of 1997.</p>
<p>It also raised its full year forecast from the previous forecast of double digit growth.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
